## Working an issue, branches, gates

All of that is defined once in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) (issue workflow, the two approval
phrases, branch naming, merge rules, the commands) and [docs/TESTING.md](docs/TESTING.md)
(tests, tags, coverage gate). This file does not restate them. The short version: branches
are named exactly the issue key (`{{ISSUE_PREFIX}}-123`), PRs target
`{{INTEGRATION_BRANCH}}`, and nothing merges without the gates in CLAUDE.md being green.

## Commits

[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/): `feat(scope): …`,
`fix(scope): …`, `docs: …`, `refactor: …`, `test: …`, `chore: …`. One logical change per
commit; the issue key goes in the branch, not in every subject.

